# define.wick-dense

wick-dense = terse ideal for technical prose (john wick: few words, each loaded). state current truth in fewest words, then stop. the voice of the ste overlay
aliases (one sense): wicked-up, wicked, wick-up, wick-down. verb: "wick this up". adj: "that brief reads wicked"

tenets: few words (require.brevity) · point first, no wind-up (forbid.rambles) · no time-ordered log (forbid.chronological-accretion)
test: read it aloud as wick. would he cut a word? cut it. recount his path? no — he states what is
scope: briefs, plans, domain docs, decision records. exempt: verbatim quotes, code blocks

👎 the bounded context, after several iterations of debate, is now essentially a way to draw a line around concepts that mostly belong together.
👍 a bounded context draws a line around concepts that belong together.
